# Reference — TA: Kingdoms Build Tree

How units get into the game in *TA: Kingdoms*: each builder
(monarch, castle, keep, trainer) has a directory under
`canbuild/<builder>/`, and every file in that directory is a TDF
specifying a buildable unit with a `[Menu] { Priority = N; }` block.
We sort by `Priority` to produce the list each builder shows in
order.

- **{{.TotalBuilders}} builders** across {{len .Sides}} side(s).
- **{{.TotalPairs}} `(builder, unit)` pairs total.**

Unlike TA, TA:K's build menu is **linear**, not a 2×3 grid — so each
builder block below is a single ordered table. The `Priority` column
is the value of `[Menu].Priority` from `canbuild/<builder>/<unit>.tdf`
(lower = appears first in the in-game menu).

Column reference:

- **Code** — the buildable unit's `unitname=` (the FBI lookup key).
- **Name** — the FBI's `name=` field (player-visible display name).
- **Description** — the FBI's `description=` field, frequently just
  the side name in TA:K (`Aramon`, `Taros`, …).

For field semantics, see the kbot docs:
- [FBI / TDF / OTA](https://github.com/coreprime/kbot/blob/main/docs/formats/tdf.md)
  — what each FBI field controls.
- [TA vs TA:K formats matrix](https://github.com/coreprime/kbot/blob/main/docs/formats/compare.md)
  — how TA:K's `canbuild/` directory model differs from TA's
  `gamedata/sidedata.tdf` + `download/*.tdf` model.

Full per-unit stats live in [TA:K unit IDs](tak-units.md).

